<p id="mwJg"><b id="mwJw">Protein diaphanous homolog 2</b> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Protein" title="Protein" id="mwKA">protein</a> that in humans is encoded by the <i id="mwKQ">DIAPH2</i> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Gene" title="Gene" id="mwKg">gene</a>.<sup about="#mwt26" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-pmid9360932_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"pmid9360932"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-pmid9360932-5"}}'><a href="./DIAPH2#cite_note-pmid9360932-5" id="mwKw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-entrez_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"entrez"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-entrez-6"}}'><a href="./DIAPH2#cite_note-entrez-6" id="mwLw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwMw"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwNA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Function">Function</h2>

<p id="mwNQ">This gene may play a role in the development and normal function of the ovaries. Mutations of this gene have been linked to premature ovarian failure. Alternative splicing results in two protein isoforms.<sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-entrez_6-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"entrez"}}'><a href="./DIAPH2#cite_note-entrez-6" id="mwNg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwOg"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Interactions">Interactions</h2>

